  "fetch": "for u in \"https://download.sourceforge.net/project/chromium-bsu/Chromium%20B.S.U.%20source%20code/chromium-bsu-0.9.16.1.tar.gz\" \"https://download.sourceforge.net/project/ftgl/FTGL%20Source/2.1.3~rc5/ftgl-2.1.3-rc5.tar.gz\" \"https://download.savannah.gnu.org/releases/freetype/freetype-old/freetype-2.3.11.tar.gz\"; do curl -sL \"$u\" | tar -xz -C corpus; done (sha256 of the archives: a1c141a3...1624a, 5458d621...6565b, cd3d8521...349ef); GLU 9.0.2 (https://archive.mesa3d.org/glu/glu-9.0.2.tar.xz, \"tar -xJ -C corpus\") for its libtess; then node tools/cbsu-configure.mjs",
  "_build": "Everything comes from the three configure scripts and Makefiles, run in the oracle container by tools/cbsu-configure.mjs (corpus/chromium-bsu-generated/build.json): the game's chromium_bsu_SOURCES with the layers PRISM has (SDL 1.2, SDL_mixer, SDL_image, FTGL; its own --disable flags for the rest), FTGL's libftgl_la_SOURCES, the objects FreeType's make compiles. Their command-line definitions are here; FT2_BUILD_LIBRARY only on FreeType's own units, as its make passes it -- and its -pedantic -ansi, which in gcc means __STRICT_ANSI__ and no `i386` macro: so ftconfig.h's inline-assembly FT_MulFix (#if defined( i386 )) is not FreeType's natively either, and the C one is. zlib 1.1.3 answers FT_CONFIG_OPTION_SYSTEM_ZLIB (ftgzip.c), as for Cube. GLU 9.0.2's libtess (with its build's LIBRARYBUILD) is the tessellator FTGL's FTVectoriser links: the libGLU it links natively is GLU 9.0.2 as well.",
